    "lawCode": "Amd §§4-100 & 4-104, rpld §4-100 sub 6, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5447\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to designating poll\nsites\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe bill gives county boards of elections the flexibility to designate\nand change polling places based on the technology being provided by\nnew voting systems.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends Election Law section 4-104 to give the county boards\nof elections the authority to designate polling stations based on the\ntechnological capabilities provided by the new voting systems.\n\nSection 2: Provides for the Act to take effect immediately.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nNew bill.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Election Reform and Modernization Act of 2005 (Chapter 181/Laws of\n2005) requires that new voting systems be implemented throughout New\nYork State. Because this systems are capable of handling ballots for\nmultiple election districts, when designating polling places the\ncounty boards of elections need the flexibility to consider those\ncapabilities and the ability of the site to accommodate the number of\nworkers and election resources (voting machines privacy booths, etc)\nin sufficient numbers to adequately serve the voters eligible to vote\nin that polling place.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
