   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to the alteration of election districts by the board of elections",
    "basePrintNo": "S5447",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5447-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4-104, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5447A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to the alteration of\nelection districts by the board of elections\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThe bill gives county boards of elections the flexibility to designate\nand change polling places based on the technology being provided by\nnew voting systems.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1: Amends Election Law section 4-100(2) to give the county\nboards of elections throughout the State the same authority to create,\nconsolidate, divide and alter election districts, which is already\ngranted to the boards of elections in the cities of Buffalo and New\nYork and the counties of Monroe, Nassau and Suffolk.\n\nSection 2: Amends Election Law section 4-104(5) to add a new paragraph\n(d), which provides that a polling place using a new, certified voting\nsystem may contain multiple election districts, provided that the\nsystem prints out separate and distinct vote totals for each election\ndistrict in the polling station.\n\nSection 3: Amends Election Law section 4-104(6) to provide that a poll\nsite must be of sufficient size to accommodate voting systems and\nprivacy booths as required by the rules and regulations promulgated by\nthe state board of elections, and that there must be a sufficient\nnumber of voting systems, election workers and other election\nresources to accommodate the number of voters eligible to vote in such\npolling place.\n\nSection 4: Provides for the Act to take effect immediately.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nNew bill.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Federal Help America Vote Act and Election Reform and\nModernization Act of 2005 (Chapter 181/Laws of 2005) require that new\nvoting systems be implemented throughout New York State. Because these\nsystems are capable of handling ballots for multiple election\ndistricts, when designating polling places the county boards of\nelections need the flexibility to consider those capabilities and the\nability of the site to accommodate the number of voting systems,\nprivacy booths, election workers and other election resources in\nsufficient numbers to adequately serve the voters eligible to vote in\nthat polling place.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone. This bill will likely result in cost savings because it will\nallow boards of elections to consolidate polling places and reduce the\ncost of running elections.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
